          "secNumber": "4.2",
          "heading": "Measurement and conservation checkpoints",
          "content": "Write down the starting composition, defect-sensitive atmosphere and powder or glass history; define whether reported fractions are by area, mass, moles or volume; and record the process history that could alter **frequency, field and electrode state**. For any local observation, describe why its sampling plan represents the part. Treat **electrode polarization and microcracks** as an explicit rival explanation and plan **impedance spectroscopy across thickness** as an independent check.",
